      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-12",
      "revision": 1379624643,
      "text": "Porophyllum ruderale, commonly known as pápalo or quillquiña, is an herbaceous annual plant whose leaves can be used for seasoning food. The taste has been described as \"somewhere between arugula, cilantro and rue\". The plant is commonly grown from central Mexico to the Andes for use in salsas."
    }
